## Testing conventions

vitest, one runner across the stack. Each package runs its own tests from its
own directory, against its own `vitest.config.js` — **don't delete those config
files because they look nearly empty.** Without one, vitest searches upward,
can pick up an unrelated config, and then reports "No test files found" while
exiting 0: a green run that tested nothing.

What ships with the scaffold, all of it real and all of it passing:
{% if needs_api %}

- `backend/test/` — vitest + supertest against `createApp()` from
  `src/app.js`. `src/index.js` is the only place that binds a port, so tests
  build an app without starting a server; keep that split when you add routes.
{% endif %}
{% if needs_ui %}

- `frontend/test/` — vitest with the jsdom environment, driving the real
  `index.html` rather than a fixture, so a change to the markup that breaks
  `app.js` fails here.
{% endif %}

